  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "#### Added\n- Stdin piping guide; stdin contract tests and derivation property tests.\n\n#### Changed\n- All six `ProcessConfiguration` derivation sites (shell middleware, `ShellRewriter` branches) now build through the internal `ProcessConfigurationDerivation.Derive` hook; `WithValidationRules`/`WithMaxBufferedOutputBytes` share one copy routine. No public API change.\n- `RetryConditions.ExitCodeZero()` renamed to `NonZeroExitCode()` (the old name meant the opposite); update pre-release call sites.\n- ADR-0001 updated; no new IVT grant.\n\n## Fixed\n- `StartAsync(CancellationToken)` returns at launch again instead of waiting for exit; call `WaitForExitOrTimeoutAsync`/`CaptureBufferedResultAsync` explicitly. Raw-mode timeouts fire mid-run again.\n- `IExternalProcess.StartAsync(config, ct)` honors `RedirectStandardInput`; a configured stdin writer with redirection disabled is a no-op everywhere.\n- Graceful cancellation is deterministic: `CancellationThrowsException` is honoured when set and never when false; interrupt faults are observed; `ProcessTimeoutPolicy.Enabled = false` really disables timeouts; no more token leakage.\n- `MiddlewareContext.Next` no longer re-runs the current middleware; sub-chains no longer leak the outer context; `ProcessMiddlewareBuilder.Build()` preserves registration order.\n- `UseDefaultShell()` uses the safe PowerShell switch set (`-NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command`).\n- `WithMaxBufferedOutputBytes(config, null)` clears the cap (unbounded) instead of inheriting it.\n- Empty-string environment variable values are allowed (clearing a variable); keys stay non-empty.\n- `AddCliInvoke` resolves `IProcessConfigurationBuilder` as a blank-builder factory instead of throwing.\n- XML doc corrections.",
